    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Description\n\nI was testing events called in form of `VeryLazy` or such thing that made `mason` won't load when I open a file that contains extension to be fowarded into the linter daemon (in this case `eslint_d` was installed with `mason`, but `nvim-lint` can't open the binary because `mason` registry path wasn't loaded yet because the plugin wasn't loaded yet) so I accidentally opened `mini.pick` and the error happens.\r\n\r\nafter dismissing the error (by pressing `ENTER`) the picker won't close or be dismissed, although we can spawn another picker and do such things without any bugs, its just the last picker won't close.\r\n\r\nbut we can close it by closing the buffer and it won't happen again.\r\n\r\nsome pics:\r\n![Screenshot 2024-11-25 at 04 07 17](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/018eafe6-7ce8-4476-89cd-770aaabe9272)\r\nin this case, `mini.pick` overlays the error message causing the error unreadable (but the window focus will be directed to the error window) so that when you press `ENTER` it will go into the error window instead of `mini.pick`.\r\n\r\n![Screenshot 2024-11-25 at 04 07 29](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e1dca396-fb5c-4380-a645-643f2ec681ae)\r\nafter the error above, the picker still exist and won't close until you close the buffer.\r\n\r\n![Screenshot 2024-11-25 at 04 07 54](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d4798f08-385e-46f1-934d-c8dcf0b5c531)\r\nyou can still spawn `mini.pick` but it will overlap the last picker (normal usage, there are no bugs) \r\n\r\nidk this might be a very edge case or so, just pointing out, I really want to take a look in the code but haven't yet figured it out (I'm new to mini environments but already moved several of my plugins to mini (like 7 plugins) so it won't grow a hefty size in my memory I can just use mini if its already available here.\r\n\r\nenv:\r\n- macos sonoma\r\n- alacritty + tmux\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.10.2\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n2. put mason in lazy load state (while an lsp or linter is already installed)\r\n3. open mini.pick\r\n4. open file that relates the linter with (e.g: ts files with `eslint_d`)\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nif there are errors we could just destroy the picker, i think...\n\n### Actual behavior\n\ndefined above in the description (with images).\r\n\r\nhere are the video observation:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2578a502-cd1e-4d70-b8cb-a87df3229aea\r\n\r\n",
